Source: morsh
Section: net
Priority: optional
Maintainer: morsh contributors <team@morsh.dev>
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13), cargo, rustc (>= 1.80)
Standards-Version: 4.6.2
Homepage: https://github.com/morsh/morsh

Package: morsh
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Description: Next-generation resilient QUIC SSH client
 morsh combines the strongest innovations of Mosh and SSH3:
 - QUIC and TLS 1.3 encryption with 0-RTT/1-RTT handshakes
 - Network roaming across Wi-Fi, cellular, and wired interfaces
 - Speculative local echo engine eliminating typing latency
 - Transparent TLS 1.3 over TCP fallback
 - TCP, UDP, and dynamic SOCKS5 port forwarding

Package: morshd
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}, adduser
Description: Next-generation resilient QUIC SSH daemon
 morshd is the system daemon for the morsh remote access protocol:
 - Stealth anti-port-scanning secret knocking
 - SSH public key and Linux PAM authentication
 - Persistent PTY sessions surviving network drops and sleep
 - Screen state tracking and instant resumption snapshots
